DATA SOURCES AND TERMS (not covered by the software MIT license)
No medical images, generated results, or trained weights are included here.
Download/preprocessing scripts preserve upstream archive contents and record
local provenance. Dataset access/usage rules remain the provider's rules.

IXI: Information eXtraction from Images project, EPSRC GR/S21533/02;
Guy's Hospital, Hammersmith Hospital, and Institute of Psychiatry.
Source: https://brain-development.org/ixi-dataset/
License: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/
Raw T1 images do not include regional anatomical labels. Supply independently
obtained annotations for the semantic prior and anatomical evaluation.

OASIS-1: Open Access Series of Imaging Studies, Washington University.
Marcus et al. Open Access Series of Imaging Studies (OASIS): Cross-sectional
MRI data in young, middle aged, nondemented, and demented older adults.
Journal of Cognitive Neuroscience 19(9), 1498-1507 (2007).
DOI: 10.1162/jocn.2007.19.9.1498
Source: https://sites.wustl.edu/oasisbrains/home/oasis-1/
Access/terms: https://sites.wustl.edu/oasisbrains/request-access/
Complete the provider's current request and data-use process. The CLI flag
--terms-accepted declares the operator has done so; it does not grant access.
The script selects MR1 only and never conflates OASIS-1 with OASIS-3.

IBSR18: Internet Brain Segmentation Repository, v2.0, maintained by the
Center for Morphometric Analysis at Massachusetts General Hospital.
Source: https://www.nitrc.org/projects/ibsr/
Downloads/terms: https://www.nitrc.org/frs/?group_id=48
Follow the upstream access and use requirements; NITRC login may be needed.
The script selects anatomical seg_ana labels, not segTRI tissue labels.

Optional IXITiny CPU smoke workflow:
IXI-derived low-resolution scans and binary whole-brain masks are provided
by the TorchIO project; these remain CC BY-SA 3.0. Masks are not regional
anatomical annotations. The download is pinned by commit and SHA-256.
Provider: https://github.com/TorchIO-project/torchio-data
Documentation: https://docs.torchio.org/latest/datasets/
Reference: Perez-Garcia, Sparks, Ourselin. TorchIO: A Python library for
efficient loading, preprocessing, augmentation and patch-based sampling of
medical images in deep learning. Computer Methods and Programs in Biomedicine
208 (2021), 106236. DOI: 10.1016/j.cmpb.2021.106236.
